 "result": "Based on the subagent's report, these are the ones not directly caused by the `partitioned=` `TypeError`:\n\n1. **`test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra`. The optional async dependency isn't installed, so this is an environment/extras problem.\n2. **`test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: `max_form_memory_size` is `None` instead of 500000. That setting depends on a newer Werkzeug than 3.0.3. It's the same old-Werkzeug cause, but a different missing feature than `partitioned`.\n3. **`test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: the subagent said this is a pytest-level failure that looks environment-related, and it didn't investigate. Its actual cause is unknown.\n\nThe report also listed `test_session_dynamic_cookie_name` among the \"other\" failures, but said it follows from the same cookie failure (it returns an HTML error page). So I'd count it under the main root cause, not as independent.\n\nThe count is slightly inconsistent. The report says 20 of 24 share the main cause and lists 4 others, but one of those 4 is cookie-related. That gives 3 or 4 non-cookie failures depending on how you count. I haven't verified the tracebacks myself, so I can send the subagent back to confirm the exact breakdown and look into `test_open_resource_exceptions[a]` if you want.",
